  "id": "COMPOUND:22287 - PROTEIN:5943",
  "verbalization": "Astersaponin F is implicated in the regulation of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP through a multi-step pathway involving dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinases. This relationship is supported by the evidence that Astersaponin F directly targets these kinases, which in turn are targeted by 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine and (3E,5R)-3-[2-[(1S,4aS,8aS)-5,5,8a-trimethyl-2-methylidene-3,4,4a,6,7,8-hexahydro-1H-naphthalen-1-yl]ethylidene]-5-hydroxyoxolan-2-one. These compounds are all potential targets of Astersaponin F, suggesting a hierarchical interaction where Astersaponin F may modulate the activity of these kinases, ultimately influencing the function of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. The evidence highlights a complex network of interactions, with Astersaponin F acting as a central modulator in this regulatory cascade.",
